 ## Background
-The Angular Spectrum Method is a fundamental technique in wave optics and digital holography. It is based on the principle that any optical field can be decomposed into a sum of plane waves (its angular spectrum) [S1]. The method was developed as an exact solution to the Helmholtz equation for free-space propagation. Specific origin details, authors, and dates are not given in the sources. It is cited in recent advances in processing and rendering algorithms for CGH [S1] and in mesh-represented hologram synthesis [S3].
